{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall present an offering made by fire to HaShem seven days</b> — He says that all seven days shall be a festival for presenting an offering made by fire to HaShem, not for prohibiting labor as on the first and seventh days. And He did not specify the offering, because He is going to mention it in a section designated for all the offerings of the appointed times (at the end of the parashah of Pinchas), just as He wanted them to conduct themselves according to them and in accordance with what I have explained (Ramban on Leviticus 23:2). And the midrash of our Sages (Sifra, chapter 11:5) is to say that we must present an offering made by fire on them from anywhere, even if we do not have all the additional offerings complete. And this is correct:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:12.024620528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}